---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy — Johannes Kroll"
  description="How this small personal website handles data."
>
  <main id="main" class="prose-page wrap">
    <span id="top" class="eyebrow">
      A LITTLE TRANSPARENCY
    </span>
    <h1>Privacy.</h1>
    <p>
      This is a small, static website. It has no visitor analytics, advertising trackers, embedded
      social feeds, account system, or contact form.
    </p>
    <h2>What happens in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      The games, hidden surprises, and email-copy button run in your browser. Game state stays in
      memory and disappears when you leave or reload the page. This site’s application code does not
      set cookies or use local storage. Fonts and images are served with the site, without calls to
      third-party font services.
    </p>
    <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Email links open your own email application. Nothing is sent until you choose to send it. If
      you email me, I receive the information you include and use it to respond to your enquiry.
    </p>
    <h2>Hosting and external links</h2>
    <p>
      The hosting provider receives the technical request data needed to deliver a webpage, such as
      your IP address and browser request information. The planned hosting service is Google
      Firebase Hosting. You can find information about Google’s handling of data in its{' '}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        privacy policy
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      Links to GitHub, LinkedIn, and client websites take you to external services. Their own
      privacy information applies once you follow those links.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For questions about this site, email Johannes Kroll at{' '}
      <a href="mailto:mail@johanneskroll.com">mail@johanneskroll.com</a>.
    </p>
    <a class="button button-dark" href="/">
      Back to the good stuff <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </main>
</Layout>
